WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:04.760
I'm Jenna Fisher.
我是珍娜·费舍尔。

2
00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:06.060
And I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金赛。

3
00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:07.340
We were on The Office together.
我们曾一起出演《办公室》。

4
00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:08.600
And we're best friends.
我们还是最好的朋友。

5
00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:12.420
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office rewatch podcast just for you.
现在我们正为你们制作终极版《办公室》重温播客。

6
00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:19.400
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.
每周，我们都会剖析一集《办公室》，并分享只有身临其境的我们才能告诉你的独家幕后故事。

7
00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:20.540
We're The Office Ladies.
我们是《办公室》女士。

8
00:00:23.850 --> 00:00:24.330
Hi.
嗨。

9
00:00:24.730 --> 00:00:26.790
I'm sitting in a different seat today.
我今天换了个座位坐。

10
00:00:27.170 --> 00:00:29.990
Getting sassy, mixing it up.
有点俏皮，换换花样。

11
00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:32.490
Is it going to bring a new energy to the pod?
这会给播客带来新的活力吗？

12
00:00:33.150 --> 00:00:33.630
Probably.
大概吧。

13
00:00:34.750 --> 00:00:35.630
We'll see.
走着瞧。

14
00:00:35.630 --> 00:00:37.510
Is it going to give me a crick in my neck?
这会让我脖子落枕吗？

15
00:00:37.630 --> 00:00:38.110
Maybe.
也许吧。

16
00:00:38.470 --> 00:00:38.810
I know.
我知道。

17
00:00:38.990 --> 00:00:40.010
Why did I sit here?
我为什么要坐这儿？

18
00:00:40.150 --> 00:00:42.510
Well, guys, things are going to be crazy.
好吧，伙计们，接下来会很疯狂。

19
00:00:42.850 --> 00:00:45.250
Today, we're sitting in new spots.
今天，我们换了新位置。

20
00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:51.310
Today, we're breaking down new leads, which is Season 6, Episode 20.
今天，我们要剖析的是《新线索》，也就是第六季第20集。

21
00:00:51.930 --> 00:00:56.450
Lady, there's only six more episodes before we head into Season 7.
女士，在进入第七季之前，只剩下六集了。

22
00:00:56.790 --> 00:00:57.670
I can't believe it.
我简直不敢相信。

23
00:00:57.810 --> 00:01:03.390
But I want to point out, we did 26 episodes in Season 6.
但我得指出，我们在第六季拍了26集。

24
00:01:03.390 --> 00:01:07.230
That is a huge number of episodes for a television season.
对于一个电视季来说，这可是个庞大的数字。

25
00:01:07.530 --> 00:01:07.990
I know.
我知道。

26
00:01:08.090 --> 00:01:09.250
We all got sick at the end.
最后我们都病倒了。

27
00:01:09.450 --> 00:01:09.990
I know.
我知道。

28
00:01:10.090 --> 00:01:11.190
We all caught a cold bug.
我们都染上了感冒病毒。

29
00:01:11.410 --> 00:01:15.590
I have a little bit of trivia for you before we even start.
在开始之前，我有个小花絮要告诉你们。

30
00:01:15.850 --> 00:01:16.330
Really?
真的吗？

31
00:01:16.990 --> 00:01:17.970
What is it?
是什么？

32
00:01:18.130 --> 00:01:19.570
I looked in my digital clutter.
我翻了翻我的数字杂物。

33
00:01:20.230 --> 00:01:20.750
And?
然后呢？

34
00:01:20.910 --> 00:01:25.010
The original title for this episode was Scavenger Hunt.
这一集的原始标题是《寻宝游戏》。

35
00:01:26.230 --> 00:01:26.750
Really?
真的吗？

36
00:01:26.750 --> 00:01:27.550
Yes.
是的。

37
00:01:27.710 --> 00:01:30.430
The table read, it was called Scavenger Hunt.
剧本围读的时候，它叫《寻宝游戏》。

38
00:01:30.850 --> 00:01:31.190
Hmm.
嗯。

39
00:01:31.470 --> 00:01:31.730
Hmm.
嗯。

40
00:01:31.990 --> 00:01:36.750
I'm telling you, sitting in new spots, trivia right at the top, what's next?
我跟你说，换了新座位，一上来就有花絮，接下来还有什么？

41
00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:44.650
Well, I'll tell you, this episode was written by Brent Forrester and directed by Brent Forrester.
好吧，我告诉你，这一集是由布伦特·福雷斯特编剧并执导的。

42
00:01:44.650 --> 00:01:51.370
I'm going to hit you with a summary now for new leads, formerly known as Scavenger Hunt.
现在我要给你们讲讲《新线索》的剧情摘要，也就是以前叫《寻宝游戏》的那集。

43
00:01:52.110 --> 00:01:57.950
Saber's new policies favoring the sales team have caused them to become obnoxious toward their co-workers.
赛博公司偏袒销售团队的新政策让他们对同事变得傲慢无礼。

44
00:01:58.470 --> 00:02:04.990
Michael attempts to check their egos and teach humility by refusing to hand out the new sales leads.
迈克尔试图通过拒绝分发新的销售线索来打压他们的自负并教导他们谦逊。

45
00:02:05.650 --> 00:02:10.970
Instead, Michael gives them to the non-sales staff who hide them around the office.
相反，迈克尔把线索交给了非销售人员，让他们把线索藏在办公室各处。

46
00:02:10.970 --> 00:02:18.810
A bunch of them end up in a dump where Michael and Dwight and Aaron and Andy further their respective relationships.
其中一大堆线索最终落到了垃圾场，迈克尔、德怀特、亚伦和安迪在那里进一步发展了他们各自的关系。

47
00:02:19.310 --> 00:02:25.190
He basically hid $50,000 around the office.
他基本上把5万美元藏在了办公室里。

48
00:02:25.470 --> 00:02:25.670
Yeah.
没错。

49
00:02:26.170 --> 00:02:27.490
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

50
00:02:27.610 --> 00:02:28.690
How is he not fired?
他怎么还没被解雇？

51
00:02:29.010 --> 00:02:30.630
How is he not fired?
他怎么还没被开除？

52
00:02:32.090 --> 00:02:38.070
Fast fact number one is a fan question from Alexandra in Huntsville, Alabama, who said,
第一个快讯来自阿拉巴马州亨茨维尔的亚历山德拉，她问：

53
00:02:38.250 --> 00:02:40.510
What exactly are leads?
到底什么是销售线索？

54
00:02:41.510 --> 00:02:48.550
Alexandra, I think this is a really good thing to start with because if we aren't clear on what a lead is, this episode is going to fall apart.
亚历山德拉，我觉得这个问题作为开场非常好，因为如果我们不搞清楚什么是销售线索，这期节目就没法录了。

55
00:02:48.770 --> 00:02:49.370
It will.
确实。

56
00:02:49.530 --> 00:02:50.890
Not to mention I counted.
更别提我还数了一下。

57
00:02:51.150 --> 00:02:54.570
And we say the word leads 33 times in this episode.
我们在这一期节目里一共说了33次“销售线索”。

58
00:02:54.930 --> 00:02:55.410
Wow.
哇。

59
00:02:55.530 --> 00:02:57.090
We really need to know what that is.
我们确实得搞清楚那是什么。

60
00:02:58.610 --> 00:03:09.710
I will tell you, according to Investopedia, a sales lead is a person or business who may eventually become a client.
我来告诉你，根据Investopedia的定义，销售线索是指可能最终成为客户的个人或企业。

61
00:03:10.270 --> 00:03:18.970
Businesses gain access to sales leads through advertising, trade shows, direct mailings, third parties, and other marketing efforts.
企业通过广告、展会、直邮、第三方以及其他营销手段获取销售线索。

62
00:03:18.970 --> 00:03:26.870
Sales people then use those leads to send sales pitch emails or direct marketing materials and to make cold calls.
销售人员随后利用这些线索发送推销邮件、直邮营销材料或进行电话推销。

63
00:03:26.870 --> 00:03:37.790
Now, several factors determine the quality of a sales lead, such as whether or not the individual or business had an incentive to offer their contact information.
现在，有几个因素决定了销售线索的质量，比如个人或企业提供联系方式时是否有某种激励。

64
00:03:37.790 --> 00:03:45.150
You know, like when they say, get a free steak dinner, if you listen to this sales pitch about a timeshare and fill out an information card,
你知道的，就像他们说的那样，如果你去听关于分时度假的推销演讲并填写一张信息卡，就能免费吃顿牛排大餐，

65
00:03:45.310 --> 00:03:53.310
those information cards would be considered leads that then a person will follow up on and try to sell you that timeshare.
那些信息卡就会被视为销售线索，之后会有人跟进并试图向你推销那个分时度假产品。

66
00:03:53.310 --> 00:03:58.530
But if you got something in return, you might have just been there for the free steak dinner.
但如果你是为了得到某种回报，那你可能只是为了那顿免费牛排才去的。

67
00:03:58.890 --> 00:04:00.530
So those are kind of bum leads.
所以那些算是质量不高的线索。

68
00:04:00.810 --> 00:04:01.330
Ah.
啊。

69
00:04:01.710 --> 00:04:03.690
You know, when you take an online survey?
你知道当你做在线调查的时候吗？

70
00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:04.250
Yeah.
知道。

71
00:04:04.690 --> 00:04:06.030
That'll generate a sales lead.
那就会产生销售线索。

72
00:04:06.270 --> 00:04:08.530
I always do the online survey.
我总是做在线调查。

73
00:04:08.650 --> 00:04:08.970
You do?
你做吗？

74
00:04:09.690 --> 00:04:11.190
You love an online survey?
你很喜欢在线调查？

75
00:04:11.190 --> 00:04:11.590
I do.
是的。

76
00:04:12.610 --> 00:04:15.070
Oh, well, this explains my spam mail.
哦，那这就解释了我的垃圾邮件为什么那么多。

77
00:04:15.270 --> 00:04:16.290
It's very full.
简直爆满。

78
00:04:16.510 --> 00:04:21.730
I was going to say, nowadays, they create sales lead by tracking your purchases online.
我正想说，现在他们通过追踪你的在线购买记录来制造销售线索。

79
00:04:21.730 --> 00:04:24.190
And then you get targeted ads to watch.
然后你就会看到针对性的广告。

80
00:04:24.410 --> 00:04:26.050
I'm a real sucker for those.
我特别容易被那些广告吸引。

81
00:04:26.310 --> 00:04:32.970
Lady, let me tell you, I watched an episode of John Oliver about third-party tracking that blew my mind.
女士，我跟你说，我看了约翰·奥利弗关于第三方追踪的一期节目，简直让我大开眼界。

82
00:04:33.110 --> 00:04:33.610
Oh, no.
哦，不。

83
00:04:33.850 --> 00:04:34.250
Oh, yeah.
哦，是的。

84
00:04:34.730 --> 00:04:41.770
So when you go on a website, when you look at something, when you fill out your information, and sometimes you get a little disclaimer, like,
所以当你访问网站、浏览商品、填写信息时，有时会弹出一个免责声明，比如，

85
00:04:41.830 --> 00:04:44.310
are you okay to accept this or fill out this?
你是否同意接受或填写这些内容？

86
00:04:44.310 --> 00:04:53.290
And you click it, if you don't read all of it, and it's a ton of tiny little words, and they say a lot in there somewhere, it's like that they can then give that information.
如果你点击了，但没有读完所有内容，那里面全是密密麻麻的小字，其中某处写着他们可以将这些信息提供给别人。

87
00:04:53.550 --> 00:05:01.390
The site that you're actually interested in, like Hummingbird Feeders, can then give your information to maybe someone who makes mattresses,
你原本感兴趣的网站，比如卖蜂鸟喂食器的地方，可能会把你的信息给卖床垫的，

88
00:05:01.430 --> 00:05:07.690
who then can give your information to someone who makes tires, and then who knows where your information is going.
然后他们又会把你的信息给卖轮胎的，谁知道你的信息最后会流向哪里。

89
00:05:07.690 --> 00:05:13.530
And all of a sudden, a third party that you don't even know has your information.
突然之间，一个你根本不认识的第三方就掌握了你的信息。

90
00:05:14.310 --> 00:05:14.470
Wow.
哇。

91
00:05:14.650 --> 00:05:15.470
It was fascinating.
太惊人了。

92
00:05:15.670 --> 00:05:19.710
So there's a setting on your phone and on your computer where you can turn off that tracking.
所以你的手机和电脑上有一个设置，可以关闭那种追踪功能。

93
00:05:19.990 --> 00:05:20.130
Yeah.
是吗。

94
00:05:20.170 --> 00:05:21.290
So I went in and I did that.
所以我进去把它关掉了。

95
00:05:21.530 --> 00:05:24.110
Oh, will you teach me how to do that when we get done doing this podcast?
哦，等我们录完这期播客，你能教我怎么弄吗？

96
00:05:24.330 --> 00:05:24.410
Yeah.
没问题。

97
00:05:24.810 --> 00:05:27.630
Well, I've bought a ton of stuff from ads.
我确实从广告里买过很多东西。

98
00:05:27.790 --> 00:05:28.150
Instagram.
Instagram上的那种。

99
00:05:28.490 --> 00:05:30.250
You're a big shopper.
你真是个购物狂。

100
00:05:30.390 --> 00:05:33.930
Like, an ad will pop up, and you're like, I got a dress on Instagram today.
就是那种广告会突然弹出来，然后你就买了，我今天就在Instagram上买了一条裙子。

101
00:05:34.330 --> 00:05:35.330
I've bought shoes.
我买了鞋子。

102
00:05:35.330 --> 00:05:37.590
I bought that earwax cleaner.
我买了那个耳垢清理器。

103
00:05:37.810 --> 00:05:38.130
I know.
我知道。

104
00:05:38.350 --> 00:05:38.970
It didn't work.
没用。

105
00:05:39.130 --> 00:05:39.470
I know.
我知道。

106
00:05:39.570 --> 00:05:40.570
Don't buy it, everybody.
大家别买。

107
00:05:40.730 --> 00:05:44.610
But I did buy that countertop composter.
但我确实买了那个台面堆肥桶。

108
00:05:44.990 --> 00:05:45.810
And you love it.
而且你很喜欢它。

109
00:05:45.930 --> 00:05:47.010
I love it.
我很喜欢。

110
00:05:47.110 --> 00:05:48.510
I got in on that early.
我可是很早就入手了。

111
00:05:48.690 --> 00:05:53.410
I watched that ad before they were even available, and I was one of the people who bought it when it was, like,
在它还没上市前我就看了广告，当它上市时，我就是那批购买者之一，当时，就像是，

112
00:05:53.450 --> 00:05:56.410
at a discount because you were helping them as part of their startup.
因为你是作为初创阶段的支持者，所以还有折扣。

113
00:05:56.510 --> 00:05:58.250
I waited seven months for that thing.
我等了那东西七个月。

114
00:05:58.530 --> 00:06:00.410
Well, you were a lead, and it worked.
嗯，你是个潜在客户，而且它确实好用。

115
00:06:00.410 --> 00:06:01.030
It worked.
确实好用。

116
00:06:01.210 --> 00:06:05.190
I have a thing that keeps popping up in my Instagram, you guys, and I took a screen grab.
伙计们，我Instagram上一直弹出一个东西，我截了图。

117
00:06:05.330 --> 00:06:06.750
Because I told Josh I want it for my birthday.
因为我告诉乔什我想把它当生日礼物。

118
00:06:07.350 --> 00:06:10.050
It's a little tiny camera that goes in your bird feeder.
那是一个装在喂鸟器里的小型摄像头。

119
00:06:10.250 --> 00:06:11.270
I sent that to you.
我发给你过。

120
00:06:11.490 --> 00:06:12.410
Oh, yes.
哦，对。

121
00:06:12.890 --> 00:06:13.250
Yeah.
是啊。

122
00:06:13.510 --> 00:06:14.290
I want it.
我想要那个。

123
00:06:14.570 --> 00:06:14.830
Yeah.
是啊。

124
00:06:15.130 --> 00:06:18.010
And then you can, like, learn all about your birds, and you can watch your birds.
然后你就可以，比如，了解所有关于你家鸟儿的事，还可以观察它们。

125
00:06:18.190 --> 00:06:20.350
I saw that in an ad, and I sent it to you.
我在广告里看到了，然后发给了你。

126
00:06:20.390 --> 00:06:20.770
I know.
我知道。

127
00:06:20.770 --> 00:06:31.370
Well, anyway, these leads from Sabre are businesses that have been predetermined to want new printers, which should make it way easier than just making cold calls.
总之，Sabre提供的这些潜在客户名单，都是预先确定想要新打印机的企业，这应该比单纯打冷电话要容易得多。

128
00:06:31.950 --> 00:06:36.670
You know, I worked as a telemarketer, Angela, for the St. Louis Post-Dispatch.
安吉拉，你知道吗，我以前在《圣路易斯邮报》做过电话推销员。

129
00:06:36.670 --> 00:06:38.250
And you had to make cold calls?
你当时得打冷电话吗？

130
00:06:38.390 --> 00:06:40.290
I had to make cold calls, but I had leads.
我得打冷电话，但我有潜在客户名单。

131
00:06:40.790 --> 00:06:47.810
They were people who had expressed an interest in having a subscription to the paper, or they were people who got the Sunday paper,
他们要么是表示过对订阅报纸感兴趣的人，要么是订了周日版报纸的人，

132
00:06:47.850 --> 00:06:50.850
and I was calling them to see if they wanted to get it every day.
我打电话是想问他们愿不愿意每天都订。

133
00:06:51.190 --> 00:06:59.510
You would have called me because I get the Sunday paper, and someone reached out to me and were like, would you like to also get the Tuesday to support the paper?
那你肯定会打给我，因为我订了周日版，有人联系我说，你愿不愿意为了支持报社也订一份周二的？

134
00:06:59.890 --> 00:07:00.250
Exactly.
没错。

135
00:07:00.410 --> 00:07:01.130
That's what I did.
我就是做那个的。

136
00:07:01.130 --> 00:07:01.970
I said, okay, fine.
我说，好吧，行。

137
00:07:02.370 --> 00:07:04.270
So now I get it on Tuesday and Sunday.
所以现在我周二和周日都会收到报纸。

138
00:07:05.070 --> 00:07:05.370
Really?
真的吗？

139
00:07:06.010 --> 00:07:06.370
Hey.
嘿。

140
00:07:07.510 --> 00:07:08.470
I was a lead.
我成了一个潜在客户。

141
00:07:08.710 --> 00:07:09.330
Well, you know what?
好吧，你知道吗？

142
00:07:09.390 --> 00:07:12.650
You helped that person bump up their sales record, too, so that person's happy.
你也帮那个人提高了销售记录，所以那个人也很高兴。

143
00:07:12.850 --> 00:07:13.050
Good.
挺好。

144
00:07:13.270 --> 00:07:14.230
So we got it, right?
所以我们懂了，对吧？

145
00:07:14.230 --> 00:07:15.150
We know what leads are.
我们知道什么是潜在客户了。

146
00:07:15.270 --> 00:07:16.250
I think we all got it.
我想我们都懂了。

147
00:07:16.430 --> 00:07:16.630
Good.
很好。

148
00:07:29.510 --> 00:07:37.070
River Valley, Oregon, and Rolla Bee from Toronto, Canada, they would all like to know what's up with the dump.
