00:14:49.950 --> 00:14:52.530
That ends my segment called My Bad.
嗯，大家应该很清楚，我们经常会调换这些开场戏的位置。

298
00:14:52.530 --> 00:14:57.390
Well, what should be very clear to everyone was that we would move around these cold opens.
没错。

299
00:14:57.710 --> 00:14:57.990
Yes.
这就是它们的意义所在，它们是独立的，不需要引出任何特定的剧集。

300
00:14:58.110 --> 00:15:03.190
That was the point of them, that they stood alone, that they didn't have to lead any particular episode.
没错。

301
00:15:03.190 --> 00:15:07.950
They were one little joke in and of themselves, and they were moved often.
它们本身就是一个小笑话，而且经常被挪来挪去。

302
00:15:08.050 --> 00:15:09.150
Yeah, they got scooched.
没错，它们被挪动过。

303
00:15:09.390 --> 00:15:14.250
Well, we had a great fan catch from Maddie B in North Adams, Massachusetts.
嗯，我们收到马萨诸塞州北亚当斯的Maddie B发来的精彩发现。

304
00:15:14.990 --> 00:15:21.530
She noticed that Jim is wearing his sport coat in this cold open with Michael.
她注意到吉姆在这个开场戏里穿着他的运动外套，和迈克尔在一起。

305
00:15:22.070 --> 00:15:26.930
She said, now, he only wore that sport coat when he was a co-manager.
她说，他只有在担任联合经理时才会穿那件运动外套。

306
00:15:27.150 --> 00:15:31.750
When he returns to sales, he goes back to his simple shirt and tie and rolled up sleeves.
当他回到销售岗位时，他又换回了简单的衬衫、领带和卷起的袖子。

307
00:15:32.050 --> 00:15:37.390
She said, I think this cold open was filmed during one of the episodes when Jim was the manager.
她说，我觉得这段开场戏是在吉姆担任经理的某一集里拍摄的。

308
00:15:38.030 --> 00:15:39.490
Yes, Maddie, you are correct.
是的，Maddie，你说得对。

309
00:15:39.490 --> 00:15:46.350
This was shot five months before this episode when Jim was still a co-manager during double date.
这段戏是在这一集播出的五个月前拍摄的，当时吉姆在《双重约会》那集里还是联合经理。

310
00:15:46.590 --> 00:15:48.030
Great catch, Maddie.
发现得好，Maddie。

311
00:15:48.430 --> 00:15:53.790
We also had a fan catch from Catlin C in Iowa who says, old tech alert.
我们还收到爱荷华州Catlin C发来的粉丝发现，她说，旧科技警报。

312
00:15:54.150 --> 00:15:59.590
In the cold open, when Michael shows Jim a picture of Johnny Depp that he took at his condo,
在开场戏里，当迈克尔给吉姆看他在公寓里拍的约翰尼·德普的照片时，

313
00:15:59.730 --> 00:16:04.910
it is a physical photo that he took with a camera and had to get developed.
那是一张他用相机拍下并洗出来的实体照片。

314
00:16:05.410 --> 00:16:09.750
Catlin says, it cracks me up that he printed out the pictures.
Catlin说，他把照片打印出来这件事让我笑死了。

315
00:16:10.130 --> 00:16:10.470
Yeah.
是啊。

316
00:16:10.910 --> 00:16:11.250
Yes.
没错。

317
00:16:11.670 --> 00:16:14.110
Today, he would just show his phone.
要是放在今天，他直接拿手机展示就行了。

318
00:16:14.370 --> 00:16:14.650
Yeah.
是啊。

319
00:16:15.130 --> 00:16:18.410
This happened a lot for Jim and I when we were working on our book
我和吉姆在写书的时候经常遇到这种情况，

320
00:16:18.410 --> 00:16:22.250
because we would bring ye olde cameras to the set.
因为我们会带着老式相机去片场。

321
00:16:22.390 --> 00:16:22.590
Yeah.
没错。

322
00:16:22.750 --> 00:16:25.630
And we'd go to the mall to the little photo kiosk.
我们还会去商场里的小照相亭。

323
00:16:25.730 --> 00:16:29.810
So we'd bring in our pictures and we found so many just like that.
所以我们会把照片带过来，然后发现了很多像那样的照片。

324
00:16:29.990 --> 00:16:32.670
Well, I have some more old tech alerts for this episode.
嗯，我这一集还有几个旧科技警报。

325
00:16:32.790 --> 00:16:33.890
I love an old tech alert.
我喜欢旧科技警报。

326
00:16:33.970 --> 00:16:34.590
I know you do.
我知道你喜欢。

327
00:16:35.430 --> 00:16:39.410
Well, this episode actually starts in the conference room.
嗯，这一集其实是从会议室开始的。

328
00:16:39.750 --> 00:16:41.250
Michael has called a meeting.
迈克尔召集了会议。

329
00:16:41.430 --> 00:16:45.410
He starts by telling everyone that the lost and found is loSt.
他一开始就告诉大家失物招领处“失踪”了。

330
00:16:45.990 --> 00:16:46.250
Yeah.
是啊。

331
00:16:46.950 --> 00:16:48.590
This really cracked me up.
这真的把我逗乐了。

332
00:16:48.850 --> 00:16:49.130
Yeah?
是吗？

333
00:16:49.270 --> 00:16:50.930
And I loved Creed's face.
而且我很喜欢克里德的表情。

334
00:16:51.070 --> 00:16:54.810
I loved his giant circle black framed glasses.
我喜欢他那副巨大的圆形黑框眼镜。

335
00:16:55.130 --> 00:16:56.030
Who lost those?
那是谁丢的？

336
00:16:56.150 --> 00:16:57.850
What is Jackie Kennedy here?
杰奎琳·肯尼迪在这里吗？

337
00:16:58.090 --> 00:16:59.170
Like, who's wearing those?
到底是谁在戴那种眼镜？

338
00:16:59.390 --> 00:17:00.230
I don't know.
我不知道。

339
00:17:00.890 --> 00:17:03.830
Stanley and Dwight, they just want to talk about sales.
斯坦利和德怀特，他们只想谈销售。

340
00:17:04.310 --> 00:17:04.910
That's it.
就是这样。

341
00:17:05.030 --> 00:17:06.690
They don't want any of this other nonsense.
他们不想听这些乱七八糟的废话。

342
00:17:07.050 --> 00:17:11.230
And what they want to know, is there any word on the new leads from corporate?
他们想知道的是，公司那边关于新销售线索有什么消息吗？

343
00:17:11.790 --> 00:17:15.190
Saber spent $50,000 on these leads and they haven't gotten them yet.
赛博公司在这些线索上花了五万美元，但他们还没收到。

344
00:17:15.410 --> 00:17:17.870
And they're not going to sit around in this conference room.
他们可不想坐在会议室里干等。

345
00:17:17.970 --> 00:17:18.390
They're busy.
他们很忙。

346
00:17:18.390 --> 00:17:19.850
Yeah, they're real busy.
是啊，他们真的很忙。

347
00:17:20.230 --> 00:17:22.190
Did you notice the dry erase board?
你注意到白板了吗？

348
00:17:22.430 --> 00:17:24.410
I did, but I didn't zoom in on it.
我注意到了，但我没放大看。

349
00:17:24.470 --> 00:17:24.830
Did you?
你放大了吗？

350
00:17:25.130 --> 00:17:26.510
Oh, you know I did.
噢，你知道我肯定放大了。

351
00:17:26.810 --> 00:17:29.710
And I got some dry erase board stats for you.
我为你准备了一些白板上的统计数据。

352
00:17:29.870 --> 00:17:30.210
All right.
好的。

353
00:17:30.210 --> 00:17:32.310
They don't quite match up with the storyline.
它们和剧情不太吻合。

354
00:17:32.690 --> 00:17:34.790
Dwight is not in the lead.
德怀特并不是领先者。

355
00:17:35.050 --> 00:17:38.730
So I zoomed in and I was able to see all of the paper sales.
所以我放大看了看，能看清所有的纸张销售情况。

356
00:17:38.990 --> 00:17:41.490
I couldn't see the printer sales, but the paper sales?
我看不清打印机的销售额，但纸张的销售额呢？

357
00:17:42.150 --> 00:17:43.310
Here's the stats.
数据如下。

358
00:17:43.510 --> 00:17:46.490
Andy has sold 18, whatever that means.
安迪卖了18份，不管这意味着什么。

359
00:17:46.630 --> 00:17:47.790
Dwight has sold 21.
德怀特卖了21份。

360
00:17:48.430 --> 00:17:49.750
Jim has sold 19.
吉姆卖了19份。

361
00:17:50.410 --> 00:17:51.650
Pam has sold two.
帕姆卖了两份。

362
00:17:52.010 --> 00:17:52.310
Oh boy.
天哪。

363
00:17:53.230 --> 00:17:54.470
Phyllis has sold 25.
菲利斯卖了25份。

364
00:17:54.470 --> 00:17:56.810
And Stanley has sold 16.
斯坦利卖了16份。

365
00:17:57.190 --> 00:17:58.570
So Phyllis is in the lead.
所以菲利斯是领先的。

366
00:17:58.570 --> 00:18:01.370
Phyllis is in the lead, according to the dry erase board.
根据白板上的数据，菲利斯是领先的。

367
00:18:01.870 --> 00:18:04.270
According to the paper sales of the dry erase board.
根据白板上的纸张销售数据。

368
00:18:04.930 --> 00:18:06.490
Printers might be another story.
打印机的情况可能又是另一回事了。

369
00:18:06.670 --> 00:18:08.470
Maybe Dwight is selling a lot of printers.
也许德怀特卖了很多打印机。

370
00:18:08.650 --> 00:18:12.530
Yeah, they were in green and they were way just tiny in the margin there.
是的，它们是用绿色笔写的，就在边缘那里，非常小。

371
00:18:12.670 --> 00:18:13.430
And I couldn't see them.
我没能看清它们。

372
00:18:13.650 --> 00:18:18.910
Well, at two minutes and six seconds, Phyllis has her Bluetooth and Jim is texting on his BlackBerry.
好吧，在两分零六秒的时候，菲利斯戴着蓝牙耳机，吉姆在用黑莓手机发短信。

373
00:18:19.070 --> 00:18:22.190
So you've got some busy sales business going on.
所以你们有很多忙碌的销售业务在进行。

374
00:18:22.270 --> 00:18:22.950
Lots of business.
业务非常繁忙。

375
00:18:23.330 --> 00:18:28.170
We also had a fan question from Alexis J in Santa Barbara, California and Katie H from Ohio.
我们还收到了来自加州圣巴巴拉的亚历克西斯·J和俄亥俄州的凯蒂·H的粉丝提问。

376
00:18:28.670 --> 00:18:31.810
In the conference room scene, Michael mentions Pet Day.
在会议室的那场戏里，迈克尔提到了“宠物日”。

377
00:18:32.130 --> 00:18:32.850
I know.
我知道。

378
00:18:32.850 --> 00:18:33.590
I heard that.
我听到了。

379
00:18:33.730 --> 00:18:34.570
I was like, ding, ding, ding.
我当时就觉得，叮，叮，叮。

380
00:18:35.250 --> 00:18:35.730
Yes.
没错。

381
00:18:35.730 --> 00:18:39.850
They said, is this a reference based on the unreleased episode or script about Pet Day?
他们问，这是否是基于未播出的剧集或关于“宠物日”的剧本而做的引用？

382
00:18:40.410 --> 00:18:42.090
We have talked about this before.
我们之前讨论过这个问题。

383
00:18:42.310 --> 00:18:45.150
There was an unproduced script called Pet Day.
有一个未制作的剧本叫《宠物日》。

384
00:18:46.410 --> 00:18:50.190
And we always said, maybe that's how we all come back together.
我们总是说，也许那就是我们所有人重聚的方式。

385
00:18:50.190 --> 00:18:52.610
We do this last episode, Pet Day.
我们拍最后一集《宠物日》。

386
00:18:52.790 --> 00:18:55.330
As if no time has passed, even though we all look much older.
就好像时间从未流逝一样，尽管我们看起来都老了很多。

387
00:18:55.550 --> 00:18:55.750
Right.
对。

388
00:18:56.190 --> 00:18:57.510
That would be so crazy.
那会非常疯狂。

389
00:18:58.070 --> 00:19:02.230
By the way, did you know that there is a national Take Your Dog to Work Day?
顺便问一下，你知道有个全国性的“带狗上班日”吗？

390
00:19:02.750 --> 00:19:04.070
Oh, I would love that.
哦，我太喜欢这个了。

391
00:19:04.330 --> 00:19:06.070
It is the Monday after Father's Day.
是在父亲节后的那个星期一。

392
00:19:06.210 --> 00:19:08.090
This year it's on June 24th.
今年是6月24日。

393
00:19:08.190 --> 00:19:08.470
What?
什么？

394
00:19:08.750 --> 00:19:14.510
I feel like I remember one year before the pandemic, we came into Earwolf and everyone's
我记得疫情前有一年，我们来到Earwolf，每个人的

395
00:19:14.510 --> 00:19:15.230
dogs were here.
狗都在这儿。

396
00:19:15.390 --> 00:19:18.470
There was a dog that always hung out here by front reception.
有一只狗总是待在前台附近。

397
00:19:18.850 --> 00:19:21.910
But Sam, has there been like a Bring Your Dog to Earwolf Day?
但是山姆，有没有过“带狗来Earwolf日”之类的活动？

398
00:19:21.910 --> 00:19:22.970
No, there hasn't.
不，没有。

399
00:19:23.070 --> 00:19:24.570
It bums me out very much.
这让我非常沮丧。

400
00:19:24.790 --> 00:19:26.610
Well, June 24th is coming up.
好吧，6月24日快到了。

401
00:19:26.710 --> 00:19:27.710
Maybe we need to get on it.
也许我们得抓紧了。

402
00:19:27.790 --> 00:19:28.850
I would really like that.
我真的很想那样。

403
00:19:29.110 --> 00:19:29.510
All right.
好吧。

404
00:19:30.250 --> 00:19:31.850
June 24th is a Friday.
6月24日是星期五。

405
00:19:32.370 --> 00:19:33.350
Put it on your calendar.
把它记在你的日历上。

406
00:19:34.030 --> 00:19:36.610
Listen, Biscuit is not good with other people.
听着，Biscuit不太擅长和别人相处。

407
00:19:36.870 --> 00:19:40.430
She doesn't like anyone or anything except for me.
除了我，它谁也不喜欢，什么也不喜欢。

408
00:19:41.610 --> 00:19:43.910
I look forward to Biscuit coming into work.
我很期待Biscuit来上班。

409
00:19:45.910 --> 00:19:47.890
Buster, though, I could just hide in my sweatshirt.
不过Buster的话，我可以把它藏在我的卫衣里。

410
00:19:47.990 --> 00:19:48.870
No one would ever see him.
没人会发现它。

411
00:19:49.450 --> 00:19:53.330
Well, if you need someone to herd the other animals, Maggie can do that for you.
嗯，如果你需要有人来管管其他动物，Maggie可以帮你。

412
00:19:53.370 --> 00:19:53.490
Maggie, yeah.
Maggie，对。

413
00:19:53.770 --> 00:19:54.010
Yeah.
是啊。

414
00:19:54.270 --> 00:19:55.450
She'll keep things in order.
她会把一切打理得井井有条。

415
00:19:56.250 --> 00:19:59.870
There would have been a joint Stanley-Philis talking head here.
这里本来应该有一段Stanley和Phyllis的采访片段。

416
00:20:00.310 --> 00:20:01.750
It's in Deleted Scenes.
它在删减片段里。

417
00:20:01.750 --> 00:20:03.830
And we learn a little bit of Stanley's history.
我们还能从中了解到一点Stanley的过往。

418
00:20:04.110 --> 00:20:04.670
Let's hear it.
让我们听听看。

419
00:20:05.470 --> 00:20:07.930
I've been here a long time.
我在这里待了很久了。

420
00:20:08.370 --> 00:20:09.210
31 years.
31年了。

421
00:20:09.570 --> 00:20:12.170
And for the first time, things are being done right.
而且这是第一次，事情终于走上了正轨。

422
00:20:12.510 --> 00:20:13.430
In all that time.
在这么长的时间里。

423
00:20:13.690 --> 00:20:17.510
I just think our new bosses realize what I've been thinking all along.
我只是觉得我们的新老板意识到了我一直以来的想法。

424
00:20:17.710 --> 00:20:20.730
The sales business is the whole business.
销售业务才是整个公司的核心业务。

425
00:20:21.030 --> 00:20:21.890
It's the whole thing.
这就是全部。

426
00:20:22.290 --> 00:20:25.850
Okay, this is why Stanley and Phyllis get along.
好了，这就是为什么Stanley和Phyllis能合得来。

427
00:20:26.230 --> 00:20:26.630
Yeah.
是啊。

428
00:20:26.950 --> 00:20:28.330
I love their dynamic.
我喜欢他们这种互动方式。

429
00:20:28.610 --> 00:20:29.150
I do, too.
我也是。

430
00:20:29.290 --> 00:20:33.330
And we found out that Stanley has worked there for 31 years.
我们还发现Stanley在那里工作了31年。

431
00:20:33.330 --> 00:20:36.670
Any wonder he is so over the BS.
难怪他那么厌倦这些废话。

432
00:20:37.130 --> 00:20:38.450
Wow, it's so true.
哇，真是太对了。

433
00:20:38.470 --> 00:20:39.030
Gosh.
天哪。

434
00:20:39.650 --> 00:20:44.250
Well, Michael has a talking head where he explains that things are changing around here.
嗯，Michael有一段采访，他解释说这里的情况正在发生变化。

435
00:20:44.670 --> 00:20:49.050
And during this talking head, we see the sales staff getting all their swag.
在这段采访中，我们看到销售人员拿到了他们所有的赠品。

436
00:20:49.050 --> 00:20:52.490
I mean, they are getting just packages of stuff.
我是说，他们收到的包裹里全是东西。

437
00:20:52.490 --> 00:20:55.870
A robe, fancy coffee containers.
一件长袍，精致的咖啡容器。

438
00:20:56.170 --> 00:20:58.530
A travel bag, like a jacket.
一个旅行包，还有一件夹克之类的。

439
00:20:59.830 --> 00:21:05.470
Yeah, this was all courtesy of our graphics designer, Henry Sane, and made by Phil Shea.
是的，这些都要归功于我们的平面设计师Henry Sane，并由Phil Shea制作。

440
00:21:06.110 --> 00:21:08.510
Dwight is going to go up to Michael and say, have you gotten the leads?
Dwight会走到Michael面前说，你拿到销售线索了吗？

441
00:21:08.730 --> 00:21:10.430
You need to let me know when you get the leads.
你拿到线索的时候得告诉我。

442
00:21:11.190 --> 00:21:13.250
He lets him know how to contact him.
他告诉了Michael该怎么联系他。

443
00:21:13.430 --> 00:21:14.370
This cracks me up.
这让我笑得不行。

444
00:21:14.450 --> 00:21:15.070
Can we hear it?
我们能听听吗？

445
00:21:16.230 --> 00:21:17.090
You got any news on the leads?
关于线索有什么消息吗？

446
00:21:18.390 --> 00:21:19.270
Okay, I tell you what.
好吧，我跟你说。

447
00:21:19.350 --> 00:21:20.990
I'm going out on a very important sales call.
我要去参加一个非常重要的销售会议。

448
00:21:21.490 --> 00:21:23.670
You get any news about the leads, you try me.
如果你有任何关于线索的消息，就试着联系我。

449
00:21:24.070 --> 00:21:24.950
All of my numbers.
我所有的号码。

450
00:21:25.030 --> 00:21:26.110
All six of my numbers, okay?
我所有的六个号码，好吗？

451
00:21:26.650 --> 00:21:28.010
Including the car phone.
包括车载电话。

452
00:21:28.790 --> 00:21:29.890
All right, Dwight out.
好了，德怀特下线了。

453
00:21:31.450 --> 00:21:32.250
Dwight out.
德怀特下线。

454
00:21:32.610 --> 00:21:34.190
You know what I wrote down in my document?
你知道我在文件里写了什么吗？

455
00:21:34.770 --> 00:21:36.890
What are his six phone numbers?
他的六个电话号码是什么？

456
00:21:37.210 --> 00:21:38.970
Does he have, like, burner phones?
他有那种一次性手机吗？

457
00:21:38.970 --> 00:21:40.570
He says, and the car phone.
他说，还有车载电话。

458
00:21:40.730 --> 00:21:42.130
Where is Michael calling him?
迈克尔是在哪里打给他的？

459
00:21:42.290 --> 00:21:45.770
I don't know, but that tells me he has seven phone numbers.
我不知道，但这说明他有七个电话号码。

460
00:21:46.030 --> 00:21:48.210
If he has six plus a car phone.
如果他有六个加上一个车载电话的话。

461
00:21:48.550 --> 00:21:48.970
Right?
对吧？

462
00:21:49.350 --> 00:21:51.350
Is Michael calling him at home?
迈克尔是在家里打给他的吗？

463
00:21:51.350 --> 00:21:52.430
What are these numbers?
这些号码都是什么？

464
00:21:52.650 --> 00:21:55.570
I don't know, but I wish someone would call them all at the same time.
我不知道，但我真希望有人能同时拨打这些号码。

465
00:21:56.110 --> 00:21:57.570
Why has Jim not thought of that?
吉姆怎么就没想到呢？

466
00:21:57.710 --> 00:21:58.070
I know.
我知道。

467
00:21:58.170 --> 00:21:59.070
That's a good Jim prank.
那会是个不错的吉姆式恶作剧。

468
00:21:59.590 --> 00:22:02.610
In Dwight's talking head, he says salesman is king.
在德怀特的采访中，他说销售员才是王道。

469
00:22:02.890 --> 00:22:06.610
At three minutes, 21 seconds, he's also wearing his Bluetooth headset.
在三分二十一秒时，他还戴着蓝牙耳机。

470
00:22:06.810 --> 00:22:07.110
Hey!
嘿！

471
00:22:07.410 --> 00:22:08.210
Pointing it out.
指出来而已。

472
00:22:08.430 --> 00:22:09.910
You thought I wouldn't, but I am.
你以为我不会，但我偏要。

473
00:22:10.150 --> 00:22:11.370
No, please don't stop.
不，请继续。

474
00:22:11.830 --> 00:22:15.110
Dwight had an alternate talking head, and here it is.
德怀特还有一个备选采访片段，就在这儿。

475
00:22:15.230 --> 00:22:17.990
It's how he's going to spend his commission money.
这是他打算怎么花佣金的计划。

476
00:22:18.510 --> 00:22:20.530
I love these new rules.
我喜欢这些新规。

477
00:22:20.790 --> 00:22:24.650
I no longer have to deal with paperwork, and because of this new pay structure, there is
我再也不用处理文书工作了，而且因为这个新的薪酬结构，

478
00:22:24.650 --> 00:22:27.250
literally no limit to the amount of money I can make.
我能赚到的钱简直没有上限。

479
00:22:27.490 --> 00:22:33.750
It is possible, stay with me here, it is possible I can make over $100,000 this year.
有可能，听我说，我今年甚至可能赚到超过十万美元。

480
00:22:34.310 --> 00:22:37.530
To finally be able to put in that pool Mose and I have been dreaming of.
终于能建起我和莫斯一直梦想的那个游泳池了。

481
00:22:38.030 --> 00:22:39.710
To drown pigs humanely.
用来人道地淹死猪。

482
00:22:39.710 --> 00:22:42.320
That took a turn.
这走向有点不对劲。

483
00:22:42.820 --> 00:22:43.840
That took a turn.
这走向有点不对劲。

484
00:22:44.440 --> 00:22:47.180
Wait, and he also said, and to cross train.
等等，他还说了，还要进行交叉训练。

485
00:22:50.500 --> 00:22:51.420
I couldn't wait.
我等不及了。

486
00:22:51.540 --> 00:22:53.840
I couldn't wait to see your face, because I did the same thing.
我等不及想看你的表情了，因为我也做了同样的事。

487
00:22:53.900 --> 00:22:55.520
I was like, oh, they want a swimming pool.
我当时想，哦，他们想要个游泳池。

488
00:22:55.620 --> 00:22:56.360
Oh, my God.
天哪。

489
00:22:56.660 --> 00:22:57.480
Oh, my.
天呐。

490
00:22:58.340 --> 00:23:02.080
Coming up, we have some sass, some major sass.
接下来，我们要看点犀利的，非常犀利的内容。

491
00:23:02.340 --> 00:23:07.000
Angela has emailed Phyllis four times asking her to come over to her desk.
安吉拉给菲利斯发了四次邮件，要求她到自己的办公桌前去。

492
00:23:07.160 --> 00:23:07.820
Four times?
四次？

493
00:23:08.180 --> 00:23:13.260
Phyllis says, if I don't have time to read your emails, I don't have time to walk over
菲利斯说，如果我没时间看你的邮件，我就没时间走到

494
00:23:13.260 --> 00:23:14.120
to your desk.
你的办公桌前。

495
00:23:14.360 --> 00:23:14.580
Yeah.
没错。

496
00:23:15.280 --> 00:23:16.500
Phyllis, sass.
菲利斯，够犀利。

497
00:23:16.800 --> 00:23:19.520
I mean, she is the busiest beaver.
我是说，她真是个大忙人。

498
00:23:20.080 --> 00:23:21.220
This is true.
确实如此。

499
00:23:21.960 --> 00:23:28.040
Well, this scene was much longer, I yelled at the TV when I was watching it in deleted
嗯，这一幕原本长得多，我在看删减片段时对着电视大喊，

500
00:23:28.040 --> 00:23:32.880
scenes, because Andy is going to liken Angela to a type of bird.
因为安迪要把安吉拉比作某种鸟。

501
00:23:33.540 --> 00:23:34.880
You have to hear it.
你一定要听听这个。

502
00:23:35.620 --> 00:23:39.440
Here is your expense report, which you signed, but you did not fill out.
这是你的费用报销单，你签了字，但没填内容。

503
00:23:39.600 --> 00:23:40.280
I was busy.
我当时很忙。

504
00:23:40.360 --> 00:23:41.020
That's the reason.
理由就是这个。

505
00:23:41.320 --> 00:23:42.120
We're all busy.
我们都很忙。

506
00:23:42.540 --> 00:23:44.760
Hey, Ange, do you mind if I handle this?
嘿，安吉，介意我来处理这件事吗？

507
00:23:45.600 --> 00:23:50.680
If a company does not move forward, it will die, like a shark.
如果一家公司不前进，它就会死，就像鲨鱼一样。

508
00:23:51.100 --> 00:23:53.400
If it stays still, it gets no oxygen.
如果它停滞不前，就无法获得氧气。

509
00:23:53.660 --> 00:23:59.040
If we stay still, we get no sails, and the money is our oxygen.
如果我们停滞不前，我们就没有帆，而金钱就是我们的氧气。

510
00:23:59.040 --> 00:24:02.080
So it's really a pretty good metaphor, if you think about it.
所以如果你仔细想想，这确实是个很好的比喻。

511
00:24:02.540 --> 00:24:03.620
For God's sakes.
看在上帝的份上。

512
00:24:03.780 --> 00:24:04.380
No, seriously.
不，说真的。

513
00:24:04.660 --> 00:24:10.380
You're trying to hover like a bird, and birds can't do that, unless you're a hummingbird.
你试图像鸟一样悬停，但鸟做不到，除非你是蜂鸟。

514
00:24:10.840 --> 00:24:11.960
A hummingbird!
蜂鸟！

515
00:24:12.160 --> 00:24:13.380
Like a hummingbird!
就像蜂鸟一样！

516
00:24:13.640 --> 00:24:15.060
You guys, I'm such a dork.
伙计们，我真是个书呆子。

517
00:24:15.080 --> 00:24:19.020
I was like, all of my worlds colliding, the office and hummingbirds.
我当时感觉就像我所有的世界都碰撞在一起了，办公室和蜂鸟。

518
00:24:19.880 --> 00:24:25.820
I want to point out also that Ed Helms, who calls me Ange in real life, who has called
我还想指出，艾德·赫尔姆斯在现实生活中叫我安吉，他曾经有一次

519
00:24:25.820 --> 00:24:27.580
me Ange as Andy once before.
以安迪的身份叫过我安吉。

520
00:24:27.880 --> 00:24:30.820
No one else at Dunder Mifflin calls me Ange.
邓德·米夫林公司里没有其他人叫我安吉。

521
00:24:31.180 --> 00:24:36.180
Once again, I feel like he slipped more into Ed than Andy, and he called me Ange.
再一次，我觉得他更多地流露出了艾德本人而非安迪，他叫了我安吉。

522
00:24:36.760 --> 00:24:37.220
Wow.
哇。

523
00:24:37.680 --> 00:24:37.980
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

524
00:24:38.540 --> 00:24:38.840
Hmm.
嗯。

525
00:24:39.460 --> 00:24:41.640
That just made me happy, so I wanted to share it.
这让我很开心，所以我想要分享一下。

526
00:24:42.300 --> 00:24:47.780
Well, speaking of Andy, at 4 minutes and 17 seconds, he's got his Bluetooth headphone
说到安迪，在4分17秒的时候，他戴着蓝牙耳机

527
00:24:47.780 --> 00:24:48.600
in his ear.
在耳朵里。

528
00:24:48.600 --> 00:24:51.540
He does, and he needs a pencil really bad.
确实，而且他非常需要一支铅笔。

529
00:24:51.920 --> 00:24:52.420
Yeah.
是啊。

530
00:24:52.680 --> 00:24:57.120
He asks Daryl if he can just have the pencil that Daryl is using.
他问达里尔能不能把达里尔正在用的那支铅笔给他。

531
00:24:57.340 --> 00:24:58.680
And Daryl's like, uh, no.
然后达里尔说，呃，不行。

532
00:24:58.920 --> 00:25:00.880
This was hilarious to me.
这对我来说太搞笑了。

533
00:25:01.180 --> 00:25:02.080
So funny.
太好笑了。

534
00:25:02.380 --> 00:25:04.660
We got a fan question from Gretchen S.
我们收到一个来自荷兰的格雷琴·S的粉丝提问。

535
00:25:04.800 --> 00:25:05.300
in Holland.
在荷兰。

536
00:25:06.020 --> 00:25:10.560
When Andy is wrestling Daryl for a pencil, how much of that was scripted?
当安迪和达里尔争夺铅笔时，有多少是剧本写的？

537
00:25:10.600 --> 00:25:12.200
Because that scene was great.
因为那一幕太棒了。

538
00:25:13.000 --> 00:25:13.680
You know what?
你知道吗？

539
00:25:13.860 --> 00:25:15.800
None of that was in the script.
那些完全不在剧本里。

540
00:25:15.800 --> 00:25:17.660
When they wrestle and go to the ground?
当他们扭打在一起倒地的时候？

541
00:25:17.880 --> 00:25:18.040
Yeah.
是的。

542
00:25:18.240 --> 00:25:23.500
In the script, it just says, Andy makes the gimme gesture as the camera pushes in on Daryl
剧本里只写了，安迪做了个“给我”的手势，镜头推进到一脸难以置信的达里尔身上。

543
00:25:23.500 --> 00:25:24.540
in disbelief.
然后就结束了。

544
00:25:24.780 --> 00:25:25.780
And then it ended.
然后就结束了。

545
00:25:26.380 --> 00:25:30.380
So all of him, like, trying to take it from his hand and then them falling.
所以他试图从他手里抢走铅笔，然后他们摔倒，这些都是即兴的。

546
00:25:30.500 --> 00:25:34.080
And I think you can see at the end of that scene, you can see Craig.
而且我想在那一幕的结尾，你可以看到克雷格。

547
00:25:34.200 --> 00:25:35.320
I see him breaking.
我看到他笑场了。

548
00:25:35.620 --> 00:25:36.800
I also see him breaking.
我也看到他笑场了。

549
00:25:36.940 --> 00:25:38.240
I see him starting to laugh.
我看到他开始笑了。

550
00:25:38.540 --> 00:25:40.760
And then he tries to grab Ed.
然后他试图去抓艾德。

551
00:25:40.920 --> 00:25:42.640
So he doesn't bonk his head and fall.
这样他就不会磕到头摔倒了。

552
00:25:42.640 --> 00:25:46.080
Yeah, I think he has to kind of do a bit of a crotch grab there.
对，我觉得他当时还得稍微抓一下裤裆。

553
00:25:46.080 --> 00:25:49.680
And they cut away at the very last minute if you check it out.
如果你仔细看，他们在那最后一刻切掉了镜头。

554
00:25:50.060 --> 00:25:55.120
I would like to point out at 4 minutes, 22 seconds, behind Daryl on the wall is a sign
我想指出在4分22秒的时候，达里尔身后的墙上有一个标志，

555
00:25:55.120 --> 00:25:57.460
that says, Nobody Talks, Everybody Walks.
上面写着：不许说话，全都走人。

556
00:25:57.900 --> 00:25:59.800
A lot of people wanted this sign.
很多人都想要这个标志。

557
00:26:00.020 --> 00:26:06.120
And I saw on the internet that NBC actually sold it in an auction they had of all the set
我在网上看到，NBC在拍卖剧中所有布景道具时，

558
00:26:06.120 --> 00:26:07.100
pieces from the show.
确实把这个卖掉了。

559
00:26:07.700 --> 00:26:08.160
Wow.
哇。

560
00:26:08.380 --> 00:26:09.260
So somebody bought it.
所以有人把它买走了。

561
00:26:09.440 --> 00:26:09.980
Someone has it.
有人拥有它。

562
00:26:10.020 --> 00:26:10.480
Wait a second.
等一下。

563
00:26:10.480 --> 00:26:12.000
Here's what I don't understand.
我不明白的是这个。

564
00:26:12.400 --> 00:26:17.940
Remember when they said I couldn't have my watercolor because they had to log it and put it in a
还记得他们说我不能拿走我的水彩画，因为他们得登记并把它存进仓库，

565
00:26:17.940 --> 00:26:22.120
warehouse in case we ever revived the show or something?
以防我们以后重启这部剧什么的吗？

566
00:26:22.840 --> 00:26:24.840
I think they just wanted to sell everything.
我觉得他们只是想把所有东西都卖掉。

567
00:26:25.280 --> 00:26:28.460
I mean, what happens if we ever want to revive the show?
我是说，如果我们以后想重启这部剧怎么办？

568
00:26:28.980 --> 00:26:30.660
I mean, they've sold everything.
他们把所有东西都卖了。

569
00:26:31.220 --> 00:26:32.580
They sold our clothes.
他们卖掉了我们的衣服。

570
00:26:32.780 --> 00:26:33.300
I know.
我知道。

571
00:26:33.540 --> 00:26:34.240
What happens?
那怎么办？

572
00:26:34.520 --> 00:26:35.220
I don't know.
我不知道。

573
00:26:36.460 --> 00:26:40.680
Maybe that's why we're not reviving it because it would cost too much to go get the stuff
也许这就是我们没重启的原因，因为要把这些东西买回来成本太高了。

574
00:26:40.680 --> 00:26:40.980
back.
当时就像是把所有布景道具都清仓大甩卖了。

575
00:26:41.300 --> 00:26:44.600
There was like a fire sale of all the set pieces.
确实是这样。

576
00:26:44.740 --> 00:26:45.400
There really was.
没错。

577
00:26:45.560 --> 00:26:45.700
Yeah.
对。

578
00:26:45.860 --> 00:26:51.500
So I found that interesting that that particular sign was sold and someone has it.
所以我发现那个特定的标志被卖掉且有人收藏这件事挺有意思的。

579
00:26:51.820 --> 00:26:56.180
We also had a fan catch from Eleanor in France for this scene.
我们还收到了一位来自法国的粉丝埃莉诺关于这个场景的发现。

580
00:26:56.700 --> 00:26:57.140
Bonjour.
你好。

581
00:26:57.680 --> 00:26:58.080
Bonjour.
你好。

582
00:26:58.800 --> 00:27:04.080
Well, Eleanor said at around 4 minutes, 15 seconds, when Andy is walking past Daryl's
埃莉诺说在4分15秒左右，当安迪走过达里尔的办公室时，

583
00:27:04.080 --> 00:27:06.900
office, I swear he says, Eddie, nice.
我发誓他说的是：“埃迪，不错。”

584
00:27:07.380 --> 00:27:10.460
But then later on, he says, hang on, Teddy.
但后来他又说：“等一下，泰迪。”

585
00:27:11.440 --> 00:27:14.100
So did he say the wrong name on one of those?
所以他是其中一次叫错了名字吗？

586
00:27:14.300 --> 00:27:15.480
Was this supposed to happen?
这是原本就该发生的吗？

587
00:27:16.460 --> 00:27:17.900
Eleanor, I went to the script.
埃莉诺，我查了剧本。

588
00:27:18.280 --> 00:27:19.880
There were no names in the script.
剧本里根本没有名字。

589
00:27:20.100 --> 00:27:22.960
I think this was Ed just kind of riffing at the top of this scene.
我觉得这只是埃德在这一幕开头即兴发挥的。

590
00:27:23.600 --> 00:27:26.580
I pulled an audio clip because I think Eleanor is right.
我调出了音频片段，因为我觉得埃莉诺是对的。

591
00:27:26.720 --> 00:27:27.460
Let's listen to it.
我们来听听看。

592
00:27:27.580 --> 00:27:30.780
Oh, is this going to be like, is the dress blue or black?
哦，这会像那件裙子到底是蓝色还是黑色一样吗？

593
00:27:31.080 --> 00:27:31.220
Okay.
好的。

594
00:27:31.440 --> 00:27:32.540
So we're listening for?
所以我们要听的是？

595
00:27:32.800 --> 00:27:35.060
We're listening for Eddie first and then Teddy.
我们先听“埃迪”，然后再听“泰迪”。

596
00:27:35.280 --> 00:27:35.620
Got it.
明白了。

597
00:27:36.620 --> 00:27:37.400
Eddie, nice.
埃迪，不错。

598
00:27:37.500 --> 00:27:39.140
Let me just, let me write that down real quick.
让我，让我赶紧记下来。

599
00:27:39.820 --> 00:27:40.200
Pencil.
铅笔。

600
00:27:41.100 --> 00:27:41.900
Give me a pencil.
给我一支铅笔。

601
00:27:43.810 --> 00:27:44.810
Hang on, Teddy.
等等，泰迪。

602
00:27:45.950 --> 00:27:46.390
Right?
对吧？

603
00:27:46.710 --> 00:27:48.790
He totally says Eddie and then Teddy.
他确实先说了埃迪，然后又说了泰迪。

604
00:27:49.050 --> 00:27:49.850
I think so too.
我也这么觉得。

605
00:27:49.990 --> 00:27:51.150
Good catch, Eleanor.
观察得很仔细，埃莉诺。

606
00:27:51.830 --> 00:27:52.530
C'est bon.
很好。

607
00:27:53.270 --> 00:27:53.710
Magnifique.
太棒了。

608
00:27:55.350 --> 00:27:57.150
That is all the French I know.
我只会说这几句法语。

609
00:27:57.450 --> 00:28:00.490
Unless I'm at a fruit stand and it comes pouring out of me.
除非我在水果摊前，那些词才会不由自主地冒出来。

610
00:28:01.350 --> 00:28:02.950
Daryl finds Michael in the kitchen.
达里尔在厨房找到了迈克尔。

611
00:28:03.270 --> 00:28:06.450
Michael's really sad because his honey and jelly sandwich has been smushed.
迈克尔非常难过，因为他的蜂蜜果酱三明治被压扁了。

612
00:28:06.610 --> 00:28:07.930
And Daryl says, you know what?
然后达里尔说，你知道吗？

613
00:28:07.930 --> 00:28:08.770
It was the sales team.
是销售团队干的。

614
00:28:09.210 --> 00:28:09.910
It was.
确实是他们。

615
00:28:10.290 --> 00:28:11.990
He didn't have to see him to know it.
他不用亲眼看见也知道。

616
00:28:12.110 --> 00:28:13.290
They're out of control.
他们简直无法无天。

617
00:28:13.530 --> 00:28:16.350
