垃圾车的司机是迈克·斯托克，你们还记得吧，他就是我们在“股东大会”那一集里的豪华轿车司机。

939
00:41:19.960 --> 00:41:20.300
Yep.
没错。

940
00:41:20.840 --> 00:41:22.320
He's driving stuff for us.
他在帮我们开车。

941
00:41:22.380 --> 00:41:22.720
He is.
确实是。

942
00:41:22.980 --> 00:41:31.040
Did you notice at 13 minutes, 41 seconds, when Michael is trying to recruit everyone, you know, we got to go to the dumpster now, guys.
你们有没有注意到在13分41秒时，当迈克尔试图招募大家，说“伙计们，我们现在得去垃圾箱那儿了”。

943
00:41:31.240 --> 00:41:32.040
Who's with me?
谁跟我一起去？

944
00:41:32.180 --> 00:41:32.280
Yeah.
好。

945
00:41:32.820 --> 00:41:36.480
His suit jacket, when the sun hits it just right, looks purple.
他的西装外套在阳光照射下看起来是紫色的。

946
00:41:37.040 --> 00:41:37.520
No.
不会吧。

947
00:41:37.940 --> 00:41:38.420
Yes.
真的。

948
00:41:38.520 --> 00:41:39.180
Look at this.
你看这个。

949
00:41:39.320 --> 00:41:40.200
I took a screen grab.
我截了图。

950
00:41:40.400 --> 00:41:40.780
Purple sun suit.
紫色阳光西装。

951
00:41:41.080 --> 00:41:44.400
It looked navy to me for the rest of the episode.
这集剩下的部分里，在我看来它一直是深蓝色的。

952
00:41:44.400 --> 00:41:47.440
But when the sun hit it just right, wait till you see this.
但当阳光恰好照在上面时，等着瞧吧。

953
00:41:47.620 --> 00:41:50.260
It has a little sheen to it.
它带有一点光泽。

954
00:41:50.340 --> 00:41:59.780
I couldn't help but laugh because I thought to our costume department and how they put such detail that Michael's suits were like a certain material.
我忍不住笑了，因为我想到我们的服装部门，他们是多么注重细节，迈克尔的西装都是用特定的面料做的。

955
00:41:59.780 --> 00:42:00.260
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

956
00:42:00.640 --> 00:42:02.360
Look at, like, tell me you see purple.
你看，告诉我你看到了紫色。

957
00:42:03.160 --> 00:42:04.040
Oh, yeah.
噢，没错。

958
00:42:04.580 --> 00:42:06.520
Yeah, that has some purple undertones.
是啊，那确实带点紫色调。

959
00:42:06.560 --> 00:42:06.840
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

960
00:42:07.020 --> 00:42:08.560
And when the sun hit it, for sure.
当阳光照到它的时候，绝对是这样。

961
00:42:08.780 --> 00:42:09.140
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

962
00:42:09.620 --> 00:42:10.820
So here's the thing.
所以事情是这样的。

963
00:42:11.020 --> 00:42:15.100
The only person who's willing to go to the dump with Michael is Dwight.
唯一愿意和迈克尔一起去垃圾场的人是德怀特。

964
00:42:15.540 --> 00:42:15.760
Yeah.
没错。

965
00:42:16.260 --> 00:42:19.440
Dwight says, you know what, I'm going to go with you because you'll probably mess it up.
德怀特说，你知道吗，我要跟你一起去，因为你很可能会搞砸。

966
00:42:19.960 --> 00:42:20.400
Yeah.
是啊。

967
00:42:20.800 --> 00:42:23.660
So we go to our dump that's really in our warehouse.
所以我们去了那个其实是在我们仓库里的垃圾场。

968
00:42:24.300 --> 00:42:28.420
And I have to say, I loved all these scenes with Michael and Dwight at the dump.
我必须说，我非常喜欢迈克尔和德怀特在垃圾场的所有这些场景。

969
00:42:28.620 --> 00:42:29.340
I did, too.
我也喜欢。

970
00:42:29.340 --> 00:42:31.680
I loved it when they said, well, this place has really gone to hell.
我特别喜欢他们说“这地方真是变得一团糟”的时候。

971
00:42:31.840 --> 00:42:32.040
Yeah.
是啊。

972
00:42:32.260 --> 00:42:34.260
Like, what did it start out like?
就好像，这地方一开始是什么样似的？

973
00:42:34.560 --> 00:42:34.960
Yes.
没错。

974
00:42:35.160 --> 00:42:38.920
Well, while they're at the dump, Michael says, Dwight, you've changed.
好吧，当他们在垃圾场时，迈克尔说，德怀特，你变了。

975
00:42:39.200 --> 00:42:39.520
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

976
00:42:39.880 --> 00:42:42.500
You suddenly care so much about money.
你突然变得这么看重钱了。

977
00:42:42.860 --> 00:42:43.040
Yeah.
是啊。

978
00:42:43.200 --> 00:42:47.960
And I love this runner where Dwight says, you know, he'd be doing so much better without Michael.
我喜欢这个贯穿始终的梗，德怀特说，你知道，没有迈克尔他会过得好得多。

979
00:42:48.300 --> 00:42:54.440
He could have taken that job at Home Depot where he could be number two at Home Depot.
他本可以去家得宝工作，在那里他能成为二把手。

980
00:42:54.440 --> 00:42:56.220
But instead, he went with Michael.
但相反，他选择了迈克尔。

981
00:42:56.220 --> 00:42:57.400
And now look where they are.
现在看看他们在哪儿。

982
00:42:57.820 --> 00:43:00.580
They start throwing trash at each other.
他们开始互相扔垃圾。

983
00:43:00.800 --> 00:43:01.940
So much trash.
好多垃圾。

984
00:43:02.220 --> 00:43:02.960
Big trash.
大件垃圾。

985
00:43:03.420 --> 00:43:04.380
Big spool.
大线轴。

986
00:43:04.780 --> 00:43:05.180
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

987
00:43:05.300 --> 00:43:09.740
That's my favorite part of this scene is all of the spool, quote-unquote, throwing.
这一幕里我最喜欢的部分就是所有那些所谓的“线轴”投掷。

988
00:43:10.520 --> 00:43:13.100
We actually had a fan catch from Michelle G.
我们确实收到了来自俄勒冈州米歇尔·G的粉丝提问。

989
00:43:13.260 --> 00:43:13.700
in Oregon.
在俄勒冈州。

990
00:43:14.060 --> 00:43:15.180
Hi, Office Ladies.
嗨，《办公室》女士们。

991
00:43:15.320 --> 00:43:20.200
Every time I watch this episode, I am oddly fascinated by the giant spool at the dump.
每次看这一集，我都对垃圾场那个巨大的线轴感到莫名着迷。

992
00:43:20.380 --> 00:43:21.980
Was this in the script?
这是剧本里写的吗？

993
00:43:22.540 --> 00:43:23.040
No.
不是。

994
00:43:23.420 --> 00:43:26.060
The spool was not in the script.
剧本里并没有写线轴。

995
00:43:26.060 --> 00:43:29.240
It just specified that they would throw trash.
只是规定了他们要扔垃圾。

996
00:43:29.820 --> 00:43:35.360
I want you to know at 17 minutes and 23 seconds, there is a second spool.
我想让你们知道，在17分23秒的时候，有第二个线轴。

997
00:43:35.920 --> 00:43:36.380
What?
什么？

998
00:43:36.560 --> 00:43:37.640
There were two spools.
有两个线轴。

999
00:43:38.000 --> 00:43:39.280
There's two spools, guys.
伙计们，有两个线轴。

1000
00:43:39.480 --> 00:43:44.500
One that they're throwing at each other and one, if you look behind Dwight, spool number two.
一个是他们互相扔的，另一个，如果你看德怀特身后，那是二号线轴。

1001
00:43:44.720 --> 00:43:45.640
Second spool.
第二卷。

1002
00:43:45.820 --> 00:43:46.100
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1003
00:43:46.780 --> 00:43:48.780
Well, Jenna, have you ever been to a dump?
那么，珍娜，你去过垃圾场吗？

1004
00:43:49.060 --> 00:43:50.720
I have not ever toured a dump.
我从来没参观过垃圾场。

1005
00:43:50.880 --> 00:43:53.320
My Uncle Carl used to drive a dump truck.
我卡尔叔叔以前开过垃圾车。

1006
00:43:53.540 --> 00:43:53.920
Okay.
好的。

1007
00:43:53.920 --> 00:43:56.460
And my sisters and I would love to ride in it with them.
我和我姐妹们以前特别喜欢跟他一起坐那辆车。

1008
00:43:56.680 --> 00:43:57.580
It was a big old truck.
那是一辆又大又旧的卡车。

1009
00:43:57.760 --> 00:43:58.020
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1010
00:43:58.160 --> 00:44:00.920
And we went to the local dump many times.
我们去过当地的垃圾场很多次。

1011
00:44:01.100 --> 00:44:02.980
I have questions before you even get to the dump.
在你讲到垃圾场之前，我先问几个问题。

1012
00:44:03.100 --> 00:44:03.240
Okay.
好的。

1013
00:44:03.680 --> 00:44:08.040
Was it a trash truck that, like, automatically put the trash in the back, or did he have to
那是那种能自动把垃圾装进车后的垃圾车，还是他必须

1014
00:44:08.040 --> 00:44:09.260
get out and do it manually?
下车手动操作？

1015
00:44:09.980 --> 00:44:14.360
Because, like, when I was a kid, they didn't have the ones that had the little arm.
因为我小时候，还没有那种带小机械臂的垃圾车。

1016
00:44:14.500 --> 00:44:14.920
No, no, no.
不，不，不。

1017
00:44:14.920 --> 00:44:16.780
You had to get out and throw the trash in.
你得下车把垃圾扔进去。

1018
00:44:16.860 --> 00:44:17.920
This was, like, old school.
那是老派的做法。

1019
00:44:18.120 --> 00:44:18.620
You're correct.
你说得对。

1020
00:44:18.620 --> 00:44:23.040
This was before the fancy trucks that have the arm that comes out and picks something up.
那是在那种带机械臂、能自动抓取东西的先进卡车出现之前。

1021
00:44:23.040 --> 00:44:27.260
Okay, because, see, I was curious, because I think if you were a kid, it would be fun
好的，因为我很好奇，我觉得如果你还是个孩子，如果他让你

1022
00:44:27.260 --> 00:44:29.160
if he let you operate the little arm.
操作那个小机械臂，那肯定很有趣。

1023
00:44:29.280 --> 00:44:29.800
Oh, yeah.
哦，确实。

1024
00:44:30.060 --> 00:44:30.280
Right?
对吧？

1025
00:44:30.700 --> 00:44:31.800
That would have been really cool.
那肯定酷毙了。

1026
00:44:31.920 --> 00:44:33.080
No, this truck didn't have that.
不，那辆车没有那个功能。

1027
00:44:33.120 --> 00:44:33.320
Okay.
好吧。

1028
00:44:33.460 --> 00:44:34.180
Predates that.
那是更早以前的了。

1029
00:44:34.320 --> 00:44:38.700
But I was fascinated by trash, and I guess I always have been.
但我一直对垃圾很着迷，我想我一直都是这样。

1030
00:44:39.400 --> 00:44:42.660
And for this episode, I have some trash facts for you.
所以这一集，我准备了一些关于垃圾的冷知识给你。

1031
00:44:42.760 --> 00:44:44.240
I love trash facts!
我喜欢垃圾冷知识！

1032
00:44:44.380 --> 00:44:48.300
So, according to the internet, and I looked on a few different sites, and most of these
根据互联网上的信息，我查了几个不同的网站，其中大部分

1033
00:44:48.300 --> 00:44:51.340
surveys were done between 2019 and 2020.
调查是在2019年到2020年之间进行的。

1034
00:44:51.340 --> 00:44:51.860
Okay.
好的。

1035
00:44:52.080 --> 00:44:52.240
Okay?
是吗？

1036
00:44:52.720 --> 00:44:59.080
So, the average American produces 4.5 pounds of waste every single day.
平均每个美国人每天产生4.5磅的垃圾。

1037
00:44:59.240 --> 00:45:00.200
Wait, wait, wait, wait, wait.
等等，等等，等等，等等，等等。

1038
00:45:00.440 --> 00:45:01.120
Every day?
每天？

1039
00:45:01.300 --> 00:45:01.800
Every day.
每天。

1040
00:45:01.960 --> 00:45:02.940
Four and a half pounds.
四点五磅。

1041
00:45:03.180 --> 00:45:04.520
That's the average American.
那是平均每个美国人的量。

1042
00:45:04.920 --> 00:45:09.160
However, the amount of trash that is going into our dumps right now is at its lowest level
然而，目前进入我们垃圾场的垃圾量处于自1960年以来的

1043
00:45:09.160 --> 00:45:10.280
since 1960.
最低水平。

1044
00:45:10.700 --> 00:45:11.040
Oh!
哦！

1045
00:45:11.240 --> 00:45:12.360
Do we know why that is?
我们知道原因吗？

1046
00:45:12.820 --> 00:45:13.420
I think...
我想……

1047
00:45:13.420 --> 00:45:14.100
Is it recycling?
是因为回收利用吗？

1048
00:45:14.300 --> 00:45:17.060
I think we have these initiatives now for recycling and reusing.
我想我们现在有了这些回收和再利用的倡议。

1049
00:45:17.060 --> 00:45:21.640
Here are the three things that make up more than half of the garbage in all of the United
以下是占美国所有垃圾填埋场垃圾总量一半以上的三种

1050
00:45:21.640 --> 00:45:22.560
States landfills.
主要东西。

1051
00:45:23.120 --> 00:45:26.560
Food waste, plastics, and paper products.
食物残渣、塑料和纸制品。

1052
00:45:27.060 --> 00:45:32.680
Michigan is the state with the most trash per capita, with Indiana and Illinois ranking
密歇根州是人均垃圾产量最高的州，印第安纳州和伊利诺伊州分列

1053
00:45:32.680 --> 00:45:33.440
second and third.
第二和第三。

1054
00:45:33.640 --> 00:45:35.080
That's per capita, right?
那是按人均算的，对吧？

1055
00:45:35.900 --> 00:45:42.100
California has more landfills than any other state in the nation, more than twice as many,
加利福尼亚州的垃圾填埋场数量比全国任何其他州都多，实际上是

1056
00:45:42.100 --> 00:45:44.620
in fact, as every other state except Texas.
除德克萨斯州外其他所有州数量的两倍多。

1057
00:45:45.100 --> 00:45:45.660
Yeah.
没错。

1058
00:45:46.540 --> 00:45:52.540
The largest landfill currently in America is the Apex Regional Las Vegas, Nevada Landfill
目前美国最大的垃圾填埋场是位于内华达州拉斯维加斯的Apex区域垃圾填埋场，

1059
00:45:52.540 --> 00:45:54.560
with 2,200 acres.
占地2200英亩。

1060
00:45:55.160 --> 00:45:55.720
Wow.
哇。

1061
00:45:56.120 --> 00:45:56.900
I'm not done.
我还没说完呢。

1062
00:45:58.060 --> 00:46:00.200
That's me turning my paper.
那是我在翻纸的声音。

1063
00:46:00.580 --> 00:46:01.940
I hope you're still with me.
希望你还在听。

1064
00:46:02.100 --> 00:46:03.240
I'm on the edge of my seat.
我正洗耳恭听呢。

1065
00:46:03.700 --> 00:46:05.760
All right, Jenna, the next part is a little bit of a quiz.
好了，珍娜，接下来是一个小测验。

1066
00:46:06.100 --> 00:46:10.680
I'm going to ask you how long it takes different types of garbage to decompose.
我要问你不同类型的垃圾需要多久才能分解。

1067
00:46:10.840 --> 00:46:11.220
Okay.
好的。

1068
00:46:11.220 --> 00:46:11.940
Okay.
好的。

1069
00:46:12.520 --> 00:46:13.820
Should we get our quiz music?
我们要来点测验音乐吗？

1070
00:46:14.060 --> 00:46:14.400
Oh.
哦。

1071
00:46:14.540 --> 00:46:15.940
I'm not going to get any of these right.
我肯定一个都答不对。

1072
00:46:16.900 --> 00:46:18.380
Sam, you're welcome to play.
萨姆，欢迎你也来参加。

1073
00:46:18.920 --> 00:46:19.280
All right.
好吧。

1074
00:46:19.440 --> 00:46:20.620
First question, you guys.
各位，第一个问题。

1075
00:46:20.820 --> 00:46:23.660
How long do you think it takes paper to decompose?
你们觉得纸需要多久才能分解？

1076
00:46:24.140 --> 00:46:26.680
Since we are the people's paper people.
既然我们是人民的造纸人。

1077
00:46:27.160 --> 00:46:28.260
I'll say two years.
我觉得是两年。

1078
00:46:29.660 --> 00:46:30.700
I'll say...
我觉得……

1079
00:46:30.700 --> 00:46:31.780
I like that answer.
我喜欢这个答案。

1080
00:46:31.880 --> 00:46:32.400
Two years.
两年。

1081
00:46:32.660 --> 00:46:33.760
Two to six weeks.
两到六周。

1082
00:46:34.320 --> 00:46:34.700
Oh!
哦！

1083
00:46:36.060 --> 00:46:36.580
Okay.
好吧。

1084
00:46:36.940 --> 00:46:37.880
Two to six weeks?
两到六周？

1085
00:46:38.160 --> 00:46:39.680
Get the pessimist in both of us.
把我们俩悲观的一面都显露出来了。

1086
00:46:39.840 --> 00:46:40.880
Coming out early.
这么快就出来了。

1087
00:46:41.220 --> 00:46:42.160
Second question.
第二个问题。

1088
00:46:42.400 --> 00:46:47.540
How long would it take a cigarette butt or a wool sock to decompose?
烟蒂或羊毛袜需要多久才能分解？

1089
00:46:47.860 --> 00:46:53.380
Well, first of all, I'm surprised that cigarette butt and wool sock decompose at the same rate.
嗯，首先，我很惊讶烟蒂和羊毛袜的分解速度竟然一样。

1090
00:46:53.580 --> 00:46:54.160
I know.
我也这么觉得。

1091
00:46:54.380 --> 00:46:56.180
They're lumped together here in this survey.
在这项调查里它们被归为一类了。

1092
00:46:56.180 --> 00:46:57.700
But I'm going to say five years.
但我猜是五年。

1093
00:46:57.920 --> 00:46:59.500
This time I'll join you and I'll say five years.
这次我跟你选一样的，我也猜五年。

1094
00:47:00.180 --> 00:47:01.180
One to five years?
一到五年？

1095
00:47:01.320 --> 00:47:01.660
Yay!
耶！

1096
00:47:01.960 --> 00:47:02.700
We got that one.
我们答对了一个。

1097
00:47:02.960 --> 00:47:03.260
Very nice.
非常好。

1098
00:47:03.460 --> 00:47:04.120
Learning curve.
学习曲线。

1099
00:47:04.400 --> 00:47:04.600
Okay.
好的。

1100
00:47:05.660 --> 00:47:06.100
Batteries.
电池。

1101
00:47:06.440 --> 00:47:06.840
Oh.
哦。

1102
00:47:06.840 --> 00:47:07.640
Oh.
哦。

1103
00:47:08.260 --> 00:47:10.200
Aren't we not supposed to even throw those away?
我们不是连这些都不应该扔掉吗？

1104
00:47:10.740 --> 00:47:11.100
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

1105
00:47:12.020 --> 00:47:12.500
Um...
嗯……

1106
00:47:12.500 --> 00:47:13.600
Ten years?
十年？

1107
